FRITZ!Box failover helper for OPNsense.

Watches a FRITZ!Box Cable WAN line via UPnP or TR-064 (WANIPConnection:1
GetStatusInfo) and pings to several internet addresses forced through
the cable gateway, while the gateway itself is monitored against the
FRITZ!Box to avoid false dpinger alarms.
On sustained failure it swaps the gateway monitor IP to a dead
address so dpinger reports 100% loss and OPNsense's native gateway
groups fail over, without disabling the gateway. When the cable line
is healthy again the normal monitor IP is restored.

Plugin Changelog
================

1.1

* Restarting the service ("Apply", reboot, update) keeps an active failover
* Uninstalling stops the service and restores the normal monitor IP
* FRITZ!Box status via UPnP without login; TR-064 login is optional
* TR-064 is paused for 15 minutes after a failed login
* No switching during the first 2 minutes after boot
* Configuration is locked while the monitor IP is changed
* Switching no longer adds entries to the configuration history
* "Restore normal monitor IP" button, fixed "Test connection" on 26.1
* IP fields no longer accept wildcards
* Less logging during an outage

